@{
    Class       = 'warp'
    Note        = 'Screen-space light bounce on D3D11 WARP with the real shaders and the real Pass class on synthetic buffers: a 128x96 fixture of one floor plane (its rays'' sky overhead) with one dim slab hanging over a stretch of it, the floor''s scene texels written as the albedo store times the light''s square root on a checker of two stores (so the floor''s own linear value is 2.56 on one texel and 0.36 on the next), the pass''s irradiance matched against a CPU reference march that reads each hit texel''s own linear scene value (its stored value squared; never the albedo target, never a quotient) and counts the rays it marched (the ramp, crossing and thickness re-derived from the rules), the store''s alpha matched against that traced count at every pass texel (the open floor''s all-miss texels are traced zeros, the sky and a block of cleared-normal floor carry none), a lamp band (stored 2.5, bounded by the clamp) and an over-the-clamp band (stored 3.2, refused) run through the same pass, the coverage''s two classes (the covered floor''s estimate carries the dim slab, the open floor''s estimate is nothing at all), the guide read back from the pass (a traced texel carries the fixture''s depth distance, every other texel nothing: the guide and the trace agree at every texel) and the clamp plus four a-trous iterations matched against an independent CPU reference with its numbers typed in the test (the final target equals it at every texel, the data marker is the reference''s traced count; the shaders'' own behaviour is decided by gi_filter_warp), the apply''s bounded addition (the sky exact, no channel past the white, the covered floor''s adds above the open floor''s zeros, the strength key''s ratio linear until the bound descales it, the data-weighted read of the four texels around a pixel against a CPU model, the slab''s rim told apart from a plain bilinear read), the engine''s special material rows (a band of the slab marked id 40 adds exactly nothing, the generic pixels beside it add as before: the apply binds the normal view), the calibrated bounce (a lamp over the floor at the default strength lifts the lit floor visibly, more than the first versions'' 0.55 did, and a flat open area stays under 1 %), the capture frame''s statistics (none on an ordinary frame; on the capture frame the reference''s traced and clamped counts and mean light), the pass''s null-with-reason on a binding it cannot read, and its timing pair''s per-run begins and ends'
    Prepare     = 'prepare_gi.ps1'
    Sources     = @('gi_warp.cpp', '{repo}/OptiScaler/ext/ffxiv/engine/GiPass.cpp')
    IncludeDirs = @('stubs', '{repo}/OptiScaler', '{out}')
    Libs        = @('d3d11.lib', 'dxgi.lib')
    Defines     = @('NOMINMAX')
    Std         = 'c++latest'
}
